  "x-closure_and_ordering_rules": [
    "capture_started is sent only after both sources are usable and the shared epoch/gates are established; no audio precedes it.",
    "capture_stopped acknowledges cutoff and confirmed resource closure only; it does not acknowledge audio drain or EOF.",
    "On mute, pause new live DGX WebSocket forwarding immediately, while an independent native IPC reader continues reading into bounded per-source queues. After a verified cutoff ACK, forward only valid retained pre-cutoff frames, then source_end barriers. Do not block the native IPC reader on remote writes.",
    "Native must trim buffers at the shared cutoff before framing. At 16 kHz Go validates each sample timestamp with checked integer arithmetic: capture_epoch_host_ns + capture_offset_ns + i * 62500 must be strictly less than cutoff_host_ns. A retained sample timestamp at/after cutoff is a pair failure. A pre-cutoff sample is valid even if its nominal duration extends beyond cutoff. Go must not silently trim or rewrite sequence/sample ledgers.",
    "source_end is emitted only after every retained frame for that same source through last_sequence has been completely written to the native-to-Go pipe; other-source PCM may remain queued. Go's remote source_end barrier follows all queued remote audio for that source.",
    "Control/stop acknowledgement may bypass PCM backlog only before a frame write starts. source_end cannot overtake same-source retained PCM. Preserve per-source FIFO and bounded queues; a partial frame cannot be interrupted or interleaved.",
    "If a per-source queue fills, fail the pair explicitly; never silently drop audio or exceed the bound. After closure-unconfirmed failure, abort remote input and discard queues; report explicit failure and do not fabricate final transcript events.",
    "A stop ACK timeout, pipe/process death, or false closure flag is a closure failure; it never becomes success because audio drained or a watchdog elapsed.",
    "After both source_end markers have passed during a normal stop, drain both remote ASR contexts to the single bounded overall drain deadline. Stop RPC/UI confirmation waits for closure ACK, not transcript finals.",
    "Source-local end sequence/sample totals count only transmitted samples after cutoff trimming; empty sources use zero for both.",
    "capture_failed is never a substitute for cutoff-bearing capture_stopped on an already-started session. If failure lacks a correlated capture_stopped, Go requests paired stop and cannot report successful closure/drain until its matching ACK arrives. A pre-start failure has no remote session to drain.",
    "A stale capture_stop response is capture_failed with the original request_id, the stale session_id, code stale_session, and closure_confirmed=false; it never changes current-session state.",
